{"html":"<div><h2 id=\"operational-guide\"> Operational Guide</h2><div>\n\n</div><h2 id=\"configure-computer\"> Configure computer</h2><div>\n\n</div><p><strong>Step 1. </strong>Connect the machine and computer with Ethernet cable.</p>\n<figure>\n  <img src=\"https://wiki.1laser.com/x-series/set-up/step_1_connect.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" alt=\"Connecting laser machine to computer using Ethernet cable\">\n</figure><div>\n\n</div><p><strong>Step 2. </strong>Go to Start &gt; Control Panel &gt; Network and Sharing Center, configure the connection for local connection.</p>\n<figure>\n  <img src=\"https://wiki.1laser.com/x-series/set-up/step_2_go_to_start.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" alt=\"Windows Control Panel network settings navigation\">\n</figure><div>\n\n</div><p><strong>Step 3. </strong>Select Properties.</p>\n<figure>\n  <img src=\"https://wiki.1laser.com/x-series/set-up/step_3_select_properties.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" alt=\"Selecting network properties on Windows\">\n</figure><div>\n\n</div><p><strong>Step 4. </strong>In the Properties window, select Use the following IP Address.</p>\n<figure>\n  <img src=\"https://wiki.1laser.com/x-series/set-up/step_4_properties_window.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" alt=\"Windows network properties IP configuration window\">\n</figure><div>\n\n</div><p><strong>Step 5. </strong>Set the IP Address to 192.168.1.30 and the Subnet Mask to 255.255.255.0.</p>\n<figure>\n  <img src=\"https://wiki.1laser.com/x-series/set-up/step_5_set_the_ip.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" alt=\"Manual IP address configuration example for Ethernet\">\n</figure><div>\n\n</div><h2 id=\"configure-the-laser-software\"> Configure the Laser Software</h2><div>\n\n</div><p><strong>Step 1. </strong>The first step is installing the \n  <a href=\"https://www.1laser.com/products/lightburn-software-pro-license-key\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">LightBurn software</a>.\n</p><div>\n\n</div><figure>\n  <table>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr>\n        <td>Run the LightBurn Installer</td>\n        <td>Install LightBurn</td>\n        <td>Finish installing</td>\n      </tr>\n      <tr>\n        <td>\n          <figure>\n            <img src=\"https://wiki.1laser.com/x-series/set-up/step_1_run.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" alt=\"Running LightBurn installation file\">\n          </figure>\n        </td>\n        <td>\n          <figure>\n            <img src=\"https://wiki.1laser.com/x-series/set-up/step_1_install.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" alt=\"Installing LightBurn software on computer\">\n          </figure>\n        </td>\n        <td>\n          <figure>\n            <img src=\"https://wiki.1laser.com/x-series/set-up/step_1_finish.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" alt=\"LightBurn installation completed screen\">\n          </figure>\n        </td>\n      </tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</figure><div>\n\n</div><p><strong>Step 2. </strong>Open LightBurn and set a connection.</p>\n<figure>\n  <img src=\"https://wiki.1laser.com/x-series/set-up/step_2_open_lightburn.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" alt=\"Opening LightBurn software to create device connection\">\n</figure><div>\n\n</div><p><strong>Step 3. </strong>Select Ruida, then click Next.</p>\n<figure>\n  <img src=\"https://wiki.1laser.com/x-series/set-up/step_3_select_ruida.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" alt=\"Selecting Ruida controller in LightBurn\">\n</figure><div>\n\n</div><p><strong>Step 4. </strong>Select Ethernet/UDP and continue.</p>\n<figure>\n  <img src=\"https://wiki.1laser.com/x-series/set-up/step_4_select_ethernet.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" alt=\"Choosing Ethernet UDP connection in LightBurn\">\n</figure><div>\n\n</div><p><strong>Step 5. </strong>Enter the default IP 192.168.1.100 to complete LightBurn network configuration.</p>\n<figure>\n  <img src=\"https://wiki.1laser.com/x-series/set-up/step_5_set_the_ip.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" alt=\"Setting LightBurn device IP address to 192.168.1.100\">\n</figure><div>\n\n</div><p><strong>Step 6. </strong>Name your laser and enter the work area — for X Series, 600 × 300 mm.</p>\n<figure>\n  <img src=\"https://wiki.1laser.com/x-series/set-up/step_6_name_laser.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" alt=\"Naming laser device and setting work area size in LightBurn\">\n</figure><div>\n\n</div><p><strong>Step 7. </strong>Select Rear Left as the origin.</p>\n<figure>\n  <img src=\"https://wiki.1laser.com/x-series/set-up/step_7_select_rear.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" alt=\"Selecting rear-left origin position in LightBurn\">\n</figure><div>\n\n</div><p><strong>Step 8. </strong>The connection is finished.</p>\n<figure>\n  <img src=\"https://wiki.1laser.com/x-series/set-up/step_8_connection.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" alt=\"LightBurn device connected successfully interface\">\n</figure><div>\n\n</div><h2 id=\"start-your-project\"> Start Your Project</h2><div>\n\n</div><p>The connection interface will display the laser status as “Ready”, and now you can start your project.</p>\n<figure>\n  <img src=\"https://wiki.1laser.com/x-series/set-up/step_9_start_your_project.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" alt=\"LightBurn showing laser ready status before starting project\">\n</figure><div>\n\n</div><p><i>\nNote: The Ethernet connection is not Plug and Play and requires manual configuration. \nIt does not work with LightBurn’s “Find My Laser” feature.  \nThe laser uses a static IP that must match your network.  \nDefault IP: 192.168.1.100 | Subnet Mask: 255.255.255.0.\n</i></p>\n</div>","toc":[{"id":"operational-guide","level":2,"text":"Operational Guide"},{"id":"configure-computer","level":2,"text":"Configure computer"},{"id":"configure-the-laser-software","level":2,"text":"Configure the Laser Software"},{"id":"start-your-project","level":2,"text":"Start Your Project"}]}